1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,820
15 YEARS AGO

37
00:01:33,110 --> 00:01:35,110
YEAR 2000 A.D.

38
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:02,470
Father...

39
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:48,560
EPISODE 12
THE VALUE OF A MIRACLE

40
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:55,270
Thanks, Shinji, you really saved us
from the rain.

41
00:02:55,270 --> 00:02:56,400
Where's Miss Misato?

42
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,150
I guess she must still be asleep.

43
00:02:58,150 --> 00:03:00,070
She's been working all night recently.

44
00:03:00,070 --> 00:03:02,910
That's right, she has a tough job.

45
00:03:03,370 --> 00:03:07,040
Let's keep it quiet so that we don't wake her up.

46
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:13,460
What are you guys doing here?!

47
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,380
Taking shelter from the rain.

48
00:03:15,210 --> 00:03:17,710
You sure you guys aren't after me?

49
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:20,510
Well, I'm changing, so if you peep, I'll kill you!

50
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:23,760
Shut up, ya idiot!

51
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:26,930
Who'd wanna see ya changin' clothes?!

52
00:03:26,930 --> 00:03:28,560
She's way too self-conscious.

53
00:03:33,190 --> 00:03:34,610
Sorry for disturbing you!

54
00:03:34,610 --> 00:03:36,320
Well, welcome, you two.

55
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:42,200
I see you're back. We've got a harmonics test
tonight, so don't be late.

56
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:43,240
Right.

57
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,990
Did you hear that, Asuka?

58
00:03:44,990 --> 00:03:46,580
Yes, Ma'am!

59
00:03:49,330 --> 00:03:52,040
Congratulations on your promotion!

60
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:54,080
Congratulations!

61
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,250
Thank you.

62
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:57,340
You're most welcome.

63
00:03:57,340 --> 00:03:59,300
Well, see you later.

64
00:04:00,050 --> 00:04:02,180
See you!

65
00:04:03,090 --> 00:04:06,430
What's up? Did something happen
to Miss Misato?

66
00:04:06,430 --> 00:04:08,390
Didn't you see her collar tab?

67
00:04:08,390 --> 00:04:10,220
The number of lines increased to two.

68
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:12,440
That means that she's been promoted
from captain to major.

69
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:14,810
Really? I didn't notice that.

70
00:04:14,810 --> 00:04:16,020
Yeah, I wonder when...

71
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:19,400
Are ya serious? You guys are pathetic!

72
00:04:19,690 --> 00:04:23,860
Don't you two have any compassion?

73
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:29,080
You know, it's a tough job for someone so young
to foster two junior high kids!

74
00:04:29,370 --> 00:04:33,160
We're the only ones who've got
any human compassion.

75
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:46,890
Units 00 and 02 are both on the edge
of the contamination zone.

76
00:04:46,890 --> 00:04:47,930
They've reached their limit.

77
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:50,220
Unit 01 can still tolerate
a little more though, can't he?

78
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:52,810
Lower the graph depth another 0.3.

79
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,280
He's almost reached the contamination zone.

80
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:04,400
And he's still getting these readings? Incredible.

81
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:07,950
His harmonics and sync rate are
also catching up with Asuka's.

82
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:10,200
Is this what you call a gift, I wonder?

83
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:13,370
It's like he was born to pilot an Eva.

84
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:15,500
Even if he doesn't want to.

85
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,460
I doubt that'll make him happy.

86
00:05:21,130 --> 00:05:22,920
Good work, you three.

87
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:27,840
Shinji, you did well.

88
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,140
What do you mean?

89
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:32,060
Your harmonics value increased by
eight points since the last test.

90
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:33,310
That's very good.

91
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:35,980
But it's still fifty points lower than mine!

92
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:39,060
Yes, but it's eight points in ten days.
That's impressive.

93
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:40,730
That's not impressive!

94
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,940
Isn't that great?

95
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:45,190
Such words of praise for you!

96
00:05:46,950 --> 00:05:49,160
I'm going on ahead, idiot!

97
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:53,700
<i><i>...and that was a postcard from
"Mr. Wah" of Tokyo-2.</i></i>

98
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:59,000
<i><i>But you know, don't get all sulky
because you got dumped by a girl.</i></i>

99
00:05:55,410 --> 00:05:59,000
Congratulations on your promotion.

100
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,540
Thanks.

101
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,920
<i><i>When I was a kid, this area
was filled with barracks</i></i>

102
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:03,210
But to be honest, I'm not really all that thrilled.

103
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,760
<i><i>And we were just grateful
if we got to eat that day.</i></i>

104
00:06:03,210 --> 00:06:04,760
I can understand that.

105
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:09,470
Getting praised like earlier doesn't make me
all that happy either.

106
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:09,640
<i><i>We didn't have the leisure to do anything
about the people we liked.</i></i>

107
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:11,970
All it does is make Asuka angry.

108
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:13,350
<i><i>Our parents are safe and food isn't a problem,
so we have a lot to be thankful for in this era.</i></i>

109
00:06:13,350 --> 00:06:15,020
I wonder why she got mad?

110
00:06:13,350 --> 00:06:20,480
<i><i>We live in a great time in which
we can really enjoy happiness.</i></i>

111
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,440
What did I do wrong?

112
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:20,810
That bothers you?

113
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:23,020
<i><i>You got that, Mr. Wah?</i></i>

114
00:06:20,810 --> 00:06:22,110
Yes.

115
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:25,070
That's because all you ever do is worry
about what other people think.

116
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:31,490
Congratulations
On Your Promotion
Celebration Spot
Reserved Today

117
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:30,870
Congratulations!

118
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:34,830
Thanks, guys!

119
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:36,700
Thank you, Suzuhara.

120
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:39,620
Nah. He's the one who came up with this.

121
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:44,380
That's right! I, Kensuke Aida was the planner!
Kensuke Aida!

122
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:46,090
Thank you, Aida.

123
00:06:46,090 --> 00:06:50,590
Oh, no, all I did was what
anybody would have done!

124
00:06:51,050 --> 00:06:54,010
But why's the class rep here?

125
00:06:54,010 --> 00:06:55,970
Because I invited her.

126
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:58,640
Right?

127
00:06:58,640 --> 00:06:59,730
What about Rei?

128
00:06:59,730 --> 00:07:01,650
Of course I invited her,

129
00:07:01,650 --> 00:07:04,360
but that girl's unsociable.

130
00:07:04,650 --> 00:07:06,820
Man, Mr. Kaji's so late.

131
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:08,530
Is Mr. Kaji really that cool?

132
00:07:08,530 --> 00:07:09,950
Totally!

133
00:07:09,950 --> 00:07:12,530
He's so much better than these dorks
that it's like night and day.

134
00:07:12,530 --> 00:07:14,910
It's an insult to compare him to them.

135
00:07:14,910 --> 00:07:16,580
What'd ya say?!

136
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:17,870
Let's hear that again!

137
00:07:17,870 --> 00:07:20,830
Is it still difficult for you to be
in this kind of situation?

138
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:22,120
I'm okay.

139
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,880
I'm just not used to being with

140
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,250
so many people.

141
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,760
Why do they have to be so noisy?

142
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:36,810
A promotion...

143
00:07:36,810 --> 00:07:40,640
That means that people have
acknowledged your work, right?

144
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:42,980
Yeah, I suppose.

145
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:45,610
That's why they're happy.

146
00:07:46,110 --> 00:07:47,860
But it doesn't make you happy?

147
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:51,200
Oh, it's not like I'm not happy. I am, a little.

148
00:07:51,490 --> 00:07:54,620
But that's not the reason I work here.

149
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:58,370
Then why did you join Nerv?

150
00:07:58,370 --> 00:08:01,830
Well, it's been so long that I forgot.

151
00:08:07,210 --> 00:08:08,880
That's got to be Mr. Kaji!

152
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:14,010
I came directly from HQ. We just
happened to meet on the way.

153
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:15,970
That's rather suspicious.

154
00:08:15,970 --> 00:08:18,390
Oh, are you jealous?

155
00:08:18,390 --> 00:08:20,020
As if.

156
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:23,350
Anyway, I'd like to offer my congratulations,
Major Katsuragi.

157
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:26,610
I guess I can't gripe to you anymore.

158
00:08:26,610 --> 00:08:28,570
What are you trying to say, you jerk?

159
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:30,190
But anyway, it's unprecedented

160
00:08:30,190 --> 00:08:33,610
for both the Commander and Vice Commander
to leave Japan together.

161
00:08:33,610 --> 00:08:37,030
That just shows how they trust you
to hold down the fort while they're gone.

162
00:08:37,030 --> 00:08:39,040
My father's not here?

163
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:41,790
Commander Ikari is at the South Pole right now.

164
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:50,050
The South Pole, a world of death
which permits no life to exist.

165
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:53,880
Or should I simply call it Hell?

166
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:56,970
Nevertheless, we, mankind, are here.

167
00:08:56,970 --> 00:08:59,180
We're living things, and we're alive.

168
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,640
That's because we're under the
protection of science.

169
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:04,230
Science is the power of man.

170
00:09:04,230 --> 00:09:09,150
That arrogance is what caused the tragedy
of fifteen years ago, the Second Impact.

171
00:09:09,570 --> 00:09:11,650
And here is the end result.

172
00:09:11,650 --> 00:09:15,110
This is a greater punishment than we deserve.

173
00:09:15,110 --> 00:09:17,320
This is truly the Dead Sea.

174
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:21,120
Yet this is a world that has been purified,
purged of the original sin.

175
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:25,540
I'd prefer a world where people live,
no matter how stained with sin.

176
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:28,920
Reporting. Telegram received
from Nerv Headquarters.

177
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:32,130
An Angel has been detected in orbit
above the Indian Ocean.

178
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:34,800
It appeared suddenly, two minutes ago.

179
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:37,010
Search Satellite 6 moving to that orbit.

180
00:09:37,010 --> 00:09:38,720
Two minutes to contact.

181
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,550
We have video of the target.

182
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:43,970
That's impressive.

183
00:09:43,970 --> 00:09:46,060
Now that's just ridiculous.

184
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:47,440
Closing on target.

185
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:53,900
Start search.

186
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,820
Data transmission commencing.

187
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:56,780
Reception confirmed.

188
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:57,950
Commencing analysis.

189
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:01,330
Was that an AT Field?

190
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:02,790
It's a new way of using it.

191
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,340
What incredible destructive power.

192
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:13,460
That's an AT Field!

193
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:15,970
It's using kinetic energy too.

194
00:10:15,970 --> 00:10:18,760
It's like this Angel is a bomb in and of itself.

195
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:22,220
In any case, the first blast was way off
and hit the Pacific.

196
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:24,470
And two hours later,
the second shot struck there.

197
00:10:24,470 --> 00:10:27,100
Since then, it has been steadily
adjusting for error.

198
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,770
That means it's learning.

199
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:32,730
Photo:
Search Satellite 7
Maximum Magnification

200
00:10:29,770 --> 00:10:32,520
N2 aerial mines had no effect on it either.

201
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:35,860
The Angel's movements
since then are unknown.

202
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:37,610
It's probably coming here.

203
00:10:37,610 --> 00:10:40,070
Yes, and next time it'll drop itself.

204
00:10:40,530 --> 00:10:43,870
So, that will give us a third Ashinoko Lake?

205
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:47,080
All five Fuji Lakes will be fused into
a single body linked to the Pacific,

206
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,660
taking Headquarters with it.

207
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:50,040
What about Commander Ikari?

208
00:10:50,330 --> 00:10:54,210
We're unable to contact him
due to the Angel's powerful jamming.

209
00:10:54,210 --> 00:10:55,800
What is the Magi's judgment?

210
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:58,380
They unanimously agree
in recommending evacuation.

211
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:00,510
What will you do?

212
00:11:00,510 --> 00:11:02,970
You're the one who's in charge now.

213
00:11:02,970 --> 00:11:04,890
Notify all of the Japanese government ministries.

214
00:11:04,890 --> 00:11:08,350
Under special declaration D-17,
provided for under Nerv's authority,

215
00:11:08,350 --> 00:11:11,770
all residents within radius of 50km
are to evacuate immediately.

216
00:11:11,770 --> 00:11:14,610
Ask Matsushiro to back up the Magi.

217
00:11:14,610 --> 00:11:16,440
We're abandoning this location?

218
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:20,910
No, but it's not necessary
to place everyone at risk.

219
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:24,990
A D-17 Special Declaration has been
made by the government.

220
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:28,330
All Lanes Outgoing

221
00:11:24,990 --> 00:11:29,000
All residents must evacuate to their
designated locations.

222
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,290
Beginning with the 6th and 7th blocks,

223
00:11:31,290 --> 00:11:34,880
move according to your district chief's
direction immediately.

224
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:38,460
The evacuation of the city is complete.

225
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:41,550
In accordance with Department Alert C,

226
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:45,510
the evacuation of noncombatants and
D class personnel has been completed.

227
00:11:48,270 --> 00:11:49,890
You're going to do this? Seriously?

228
00:11:49,890 --> 00:11:51,690
Yes, I am.

229
00:11:51,690 --> 00:11:55,360
You're going to throw away all three Evas
with your selfish decision?

230
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:58,480
The chance of success is only 0.00001%!

231
00:11:58,780 --> 00:12:00,150
That's not even one in ten thousand!

232
00:12:01,070 --> 00:12:04,620
It's not zero. I'm just banking on the Evas.

233
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:06,200
Major Katsuragi!

234
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,790
I am currently in charge.

235
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:12,960
I want to do whatever I can.

236
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:15,080
Destroying Angels is my duty.

237
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:17,960
Your duty? Don't make me laugh.

238
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:19,550
This is for your own sake, isn't it?

239
00:12:19,550 --> 00:12:21,880
Your revenge against the Angels!

240
00:12:31,270 --> 00:12:32,690
WHAAAAAAT?

241
00:12:32,690 --> 00:12:34,940
Catch it in our hands?

242
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:38,070
That's right. We'll position the Evas
in the estimated drop zone.

243
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:42,320
You'll catch it while maintaining your
AT Fields at full strength.

244
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:45,320
What if the Angel is far off course?

245
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,910
We'll be out of luck, then.

246
00:12:46,910 --> 00:12:49,240
What if the Evas aren't able
to withstand the impact?

247
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:51,000
We're out of luck then too.

248
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,080
Our chance of success?

249
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:55,330
God only knows, is all I can say.

250
00:12:55,330 --> 00:12:58,380
If we succeed, it'll truly be a miracle.

251
00:12:58,380 --> 00:13:02,340
The only miracles with any value
are the ones you work.

252
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:04,930
Meaning, make it work somehow?

253
00:13:04,930 --> 00:13:08,800
I'm sorry, but we have no other options
for this operation.

254
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:11,470
How can you call this an operation?!

255
00:13:11,470 --> 00:13:13,730
You're right, we really can't.

256
00:13:13,730 --> 00:13:15,850
So if you don't want to, you can refuse.

257
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,730
Are you all okay with this?

258
00:13:22,230 --> 00:13:26,160
Regulations say you're technically supposed
to write a will. What do you want to do?

259
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:29,120
That's fine, I don't plan on needing one.

260
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:31,830
I'm fine too. I have no need.

261
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:33,750
I'm also fine.

262
00:13:34,790 --> 00:13:36,670
I'm sorry.

263
00:13:36,670 --> 00:13:38,750
Once this is over, I'll treat everyone
to a steak dinner!

264
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:39,920
What? Really?

265
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,090
I promise.

266
00:13:41,090 --> 00:13:42,210
Yay!

267
00:13:42,210 --> 00:13:43,710
Don't forget!

268
00:13:43,710 --> 00:13:45,300
You can count on it.

269
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:53,970
So I suppose steak defines a great dinner.

270
00:13:53,970 --> 00:13:57,480
Does she think a kid these days
would be impressed with steak?

271
00:13:57,480 --> 00:14:01,320
That's why I say the Second Impact generation
has really cheap standards.

272
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:03,980
She can't help it.

273
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:08,110
What was with that "Yay!"?
Pretending you're so happy!

274
00:14:08,110 --> 00:14:12,240
If it helps Miss Misato feel good about
being in command, what's wrong with that?

275
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:15,910
Now, since she's going to treat us,

276
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:15,450
Tokyo Gourmet

277
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:19,750
I wonder where we should have her take us?

278
00:14:19,750 --> 00:14:22,380
You're coming with us this time.

279
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:24,050
I'm not going.

280
00:14:24,050 --> 00:14:25,420
Why not?

281
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:28,130
I don't like meat.

282
00:14:28,550 --> 00:14:31,600
Because of the Angel's radio disturbance,
the target has been lost.

283
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:34,520
We can't determine the exact location,

284
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:36,350
but based on the data up until we lost it,

285
00:14:36,350 --> 00:14:39,190
the estimated point of impact
calculated by the Magi

286
00:14:39,190 --> 00:14:40,270
is here.

287
00:14:40,270 --> 00:14:42,730
The range is this wide?

288
00:14:42,730 --> 00:14:45,030
The distance from one side
to the other is enormous.

289
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:47,950
Given the size of the target's AT Field,

290
00:14:47,950 --> 00:14:51,660
it could totally annihilate HQ by hitting
anywhere in this zone.

291
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:55,370
Given that, we'll station the Evas
at each of these three points.

292
00:14:55,370 --> 00:14:57,160
On what grounds is this dispersal based?

293
00:14:57,910 --> 00:14:59,040
Intuition.

294
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:00,080
Intuition?

295
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:02,080
Yes, a woman's intuition.

296
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:03,670
How slipshod!

297
00:15:03,670 --> 00:15:07,010
I can see our miracle getting further
and further away.

298
00:15:07,010 --> 00:15:10,630
Miss Misato has never won the lottery.

299
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:14,010
Say...

300
00:15:14,010 --> 00:15:15,640
What?

301
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:17,560
Asuka, why do you pilot an Eva?

302
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:21,810
To exhibit my talent to the world, of course.

303
00:15:21,810 --> 00:15:23,400
You mean to prove that you exist?

304
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,230
Yeah, something like that.

305
00:15:25,940 --> 00:15:27,820
You're not going to ask her?

306
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:31,530
I've asked Ayanami before.

307
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:34,950
My, how intimate the two of you are.

308
00:15:34,950 --> 00:15:36,740
It's not like that.

309
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:38,620
Then what about you, Shinji?

310
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:40,710
I don't know.

311
00:15:40,710 --> 00:15:43,670
You don't know? What are you, stupid?

312
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:45,670
Maybe I am.

313
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:50,340
You really are stupid.

314
00:15:51,430 --> 00:15:54,300
One hundred twenty minutes
to estimated time of impact.

315
00:15:55,510 --> 00:15:57,310
You all evacuate too.

316
00:15:57,310 --> 00:15:59,270
I can take care of this myself.

317
00:15:59,270 --> 00:16:01,730
No, this is our job as well.

318
00:16:01,730 --> 00:16:04,610
We can't let the kids risk
their lives by themselves.

319
00:16:05,610 --> 00:16:07,230
They'll be fine.

320
00:16:07,730 --> 00:16:09,610
Even if the Evas are badly damaged,

321
00:16:09,610 --> 00:16:12,320
their AT Fields will protect the kids.

322
00:16:12,820 --> 00:16:15,570
Inside an Eva is the safest place to be.

323
00:16:22,330 --> 00:16:28,130
Shinji, yesterday you asked me
why I joined Nerv.

324
00:16:29,340 --> 00:16:32,720
My father was a man who lived
for his research,

325
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:35,340
for his dreams, to the exclusion of all else.

326
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:37,640
I could never forgive him for that.

327
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,220
I even hated him.

328
00:16:40,270 --> 00:16:42,140
Just like my father.

329
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:47,150
He never took care of me,
my mother or the family.

330
00:16:47,150 --> 00:16:49,940
His friends always said he was
very sensitive and delicate.

331
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:53,990
But the truth was that he was just a weak person

332
00:16:53,990 --> 00:16:58,160
running away from reality,
the reality called his family.

333
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:00,490
He was like a kid.

334
00:17:01,410 --> 00:17:04,580
I readily agreed with my mother
when she decided to divorce him,

335
00:17:05,250 --> 00:17:08,130
because she was always crying.

336
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:10,250
It seemed to have come as a shock to him,

337
00:17:10,250 --> 00:17:13,130
but at the time, I laughed at him because I felt
he'd brought it on himself.

338
00:17:13,130 --> 00:17:18,220
But he sacrificed himself to
save my life at the end.

339
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:21,350
Back during the Second Impact.

340
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:27,190
Then, I didn't know whether I hated him
or loved him.

341
00:17:27,190 --> 00:17:29,190
The only thing that was clear to me

342
00:17:29,190 --> 00:17:32,030
was I wanted to destroy the Angels
who caused the Second Impact.

343
00:17:32,030 --> 00:17:34,110
So in order to do that, I joined Nerv.

344
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:40,200
In the end, maybe I just want to
get revenge on my father,

345
00:17:40,450 --> 00:17:42,870
so that I can free myself of him.

346
00:17:42,870 --> 00:17:46,080
I mustn't run away. I mustn't run away.
I mustn't run away.

347
00:17:46,790 --> 00:17:48,330
Right.

348
00:17:48,330 --> 00:17:49,960
I must not run away.

349
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:52,590
Target has been sighted
at maximum magnification.

350
00:17:52,590 --> 00:17:54,720
Distance is approximately 25,000.

351
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:56,260
Here it comes.

352
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,510
All Evas, start positions.

353
00:18:05,930 --> 00:18:09,610
All we have is a rough estimated trajectory
from optical sightings.

354
00:18:09,610 --> 00:18:12,940
So the Magi will guide you until
the distance is 10,000 meters.

355
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:15,740
After that, use your own judgment.

356
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:18,450
I'm leaving it all to you.

357
00:18:18,450 --> 00:18:20,870
Maximum Magnification
Relay: Optical observation Post 3

358
00:18:18,450 --> 00:18:20,870
Angel approaching, approximate
distance 20,000.

359
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:23,240
Commence operation.

360
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:24,040
Here we go.

361
00:18:27,250 --> 00:18:28,210
Start!

362
00:18:44,430 --> 00:18:45,970
Distance 12,000!

363
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:57,440
Field at maximum!

364
00:19:16,710 --> 00:19:18,800
Unit 02! Field to maximum!

365
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:19,880
I'm doing it!

366
00:19:24,550 --> 00:19:25,180
Now!

367
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:32,560
Bastard!

368
00:20:05,390 --> 00:20:07,720
Our wireless communications
have been restored.

369
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:10,060
We're receiving a message from
Commander Ikari at the South Pole.

370
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:12,020
Connect him here.

371
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:12,480
Yes, Ma'am.

372
00:20:13,690 --> 00:20:15,560
I'm very sorry, Sir.

373
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:19,320
My selfish decision has caused
Unit 01 to incur damage.

374
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:22,030
The responsibility is entirely mine.

375
00:20:22,030 --> 00:20:25,620
That is not a problem.
Destroying Angels is the Evas' purpose.

376
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:28,370
In fact, we are fortunate to have sustained
such minimal damage.

377
00:20:28,370 --> 00:20:31,460
Yes, excellent work, Major Katsuragi.

378
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:32,710
Thank you, Sir.

379
00:20:32,710 --> 00:20:35,290
By the way, is the pilot of Unit 01 there?

380
00:20:36,130 --> 00:20:37,340
Yes, Sir!

381
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:40,130
I've received the report. Good work, Shinji.

382
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:43,880
Yes, Sir.

383
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:46,800
Now, Major Katsuragi, I'll leave
the rest in your hands.

384
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:48,050
Yes, Sir.

385
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:50,100
All Lanes Incoming

386
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:55,810
New Tokyo-3 Loop 7

387
00:20:55,810 --> 00:20:59,440
Next station is New Miyanoshita,
New Miyanoshita.

388
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:01,570
The exit will switch to the left side
at the next station.

389
00:21:01,570 --> 00:21:04,280
Now you're going to have to keep your promise.

390
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:05,740
Of course!

391
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:09,240
I withdrew a fortune, so I can even handle
a full-course dinner.

392
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:10,950
Though it's before payday...

393
00:21:10,950 --> 00:21:13,450
Ramen

394
00:21:13,410 --> 00:21:16,500
We know the state of your wallet.

395
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:18,080
You can take it easy.

396
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:21,550
And Miss Perfect said she'd join us
if it was for ramen noodles.

397
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:23,840
I'll have a garlic ramen with no roast pork.

398
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:26,010
I'll have shark fin with roast pork. Large!

399
00:21:26,010 --> 00:21:28,300
There you go, one shark fin with roast pork!

400
00:21:29,180 --> 00:21:31,390
Say, Miss Misato?

401
00:21:31,390 --> 00:21:32,720
What?

402
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:36,230
When I heard my father's words earlier,

403
00:21:36,230 --> 00:21:40,230
I think I finally understood what it's like
to feel happy when you're praised.

404
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:44,190
And I also realized

405
00:21:44,190 --> 00:21:49,780
that maybe I pilot the Eva because I wanted
to hear those words from him.

406
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:53,200
You're piloting for something like that?

407
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:56,870
You really are stupid.

408
00:21:57,170 --> 00:22:00,630
TO BE CONTINUED

409
00:23:06,070 --> 00:23:06,900
PREVIEW

410
00:23:07,490 --> 00:23:10,610
An incident occurs during
a simulation plug experiment,

411
00:23:10,610 --> 00:23:12,990
the underground faciities are corrupted
one after another,

412
00:23:12,990 --> 00:23:15,620
and finally Nerv is confronted with making
the decision to self-destruct.

413
00:23:15,620 --> 00:23:18,000
Next episode: "Angel Invasion"

414
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,370
And expect more fan service next time too!

415
00:23:18,250 --> 00:23:21,080
ANGEL INVASION
